// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: division by zero
//
// The VM rejects a zero divisor for floats as well as for ints, even though
// IEEE-754 would give inf. The C backend only checked the int case and printed
// `inf`, so `1.0 / 0.0` meant different things in the two backends (S14).
//
// This pins the current rule, not a settled design: ARCHITECTURE.md does not say
// whether a float division by zero should be an error or inf. Whichever way
// Phase 2 decides, both backends must change together.
fn main() {
    let z = 0.0
    print(1.0 / z)
}
